5417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547943 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c889ce98-c36c-5100-9ccc-2833887780d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547957 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547957 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547957 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547957 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547957 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dbb704d4-511c-5244-871d-d498a47768aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548021 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548021 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548021 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548021 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\theta +{e}^{\\theta }$ for $-\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548021 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8023cebc-048b-5288-9c32-1da095db126f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548021 #edb/ref 1074 "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\theta +{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=1+{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\theta +{e}^{\\theta })^{2}+(1+{e}^{\\theta })^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2\\theta {e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }+1+2{e}^{\\theta }+{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}+2{e}^{\\theta }(\\theta +1)+2{e}^{2\\theta }+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548044 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548044 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548044 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548044 #edb/ref 1071 "In a factory, the average amount of sugar in a cookie is $15$ grams. However, $10%$ of cookies contain no more than $14$ grams of sugar. Assuming that the amount of sugar in each cookie is normally distributed, find the standard deviation of the amount of sugar in a cookie, rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.10\\,$ | $\\,0.15\\,$ | $\\,0.20\\,$ | $\\,0.25\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-2.3263\\,$ | $\\,-1.8808\\,$ | $\\,-1.6449\\,$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548044 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b642f61b-90d3-52e8-a698-ed0e6fdd52ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548044 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $X$ represent the amount (in grams) of sugar in a cookie. Then we have $X∼N(15,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X\\le 14)=0.10.$ Converting $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 14) & =0.10 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{14-15}{\\sigma }) & =0.10 \\\\ Φ(-\\frac{1}{\\sigma }) & =0.10 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.10).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.10)=-1.2816.\n$$\n\nFinally then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sigma } & =-1.2816 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sigma } & =1.2816 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{1}{1.2816} \\\\  & ≈0.78.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548079 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548079 #edb/ref 1069 "q-353482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548079 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548079 #edb/ref 1071 "The subscriber count $P(t)$ of a streaming service follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=2P(5\\,000-P),\\,P(0)=300.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the subscriber count growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fbdb7241-60ea-5f22-afcd-5e46de779c9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548079 #edb/ref 1074 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](images/90/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=5000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $5000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5000=2500.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548093 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548093 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "284b50fd-d719-5102-8733-5376d2d513e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548093 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186547038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548105 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548105 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "576a51b8-08b4-57e9-9da7-c6ba4b57ef63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548105 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548119 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548119 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6ce11fb7-1ed0-50ca-8962-d9ee890ba212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548119 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186548021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548143 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186548119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548143 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a48aca1d-b9af-5eb7-9522-d31ba40b69ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548143 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186548079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548153 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ba6e4c6c-2798-534e-907b-4117098421dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548153 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186548044 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
